":"which they partition (a self-loop is in no block). Blocks are ordered by their smallest edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position, each listing its edges in ascending position. An isolated vertex, or one with only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loops, is in no block.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"biconnectedComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BiconnectedComponents","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity21BiconnectedComponentsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"biconnectedComponents()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/kEdgeConnectedComponents(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kedgeconnectedcomponents(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kEdgeConnectedComponents(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-edge-connected components: the classes of vertices joined pairwise by at least "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge-disjoint paths in the whole graph, ordered as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"connectedComponents()"},{"type":"text","text":". Parallel edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are separate paths and self-loops count for nothing. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k = 1"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the connected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k = 2"},{"type":"text","text":" the bi-edge-connected ones, each in O(n + m); for larger k, at most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2n unit-capacity flows, each stopped after k augmenting paths: O(k n (n + m))."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func",